    description: "Residual of WI-nakur (branch jgstern-agent/fix/nakur): the shapes hypergumbo_core.value_flow deliberately REFUSES, which therefore still hide producer values from the L3 registry gates and from the depends_on producer-set scan. Each refusal is sound (the gate stays silent rather than reporting an incomplete set), so each is a remaining blind spot, not a false claim.\n\nMeasured on the live tree at the branch head, `find_producer_coherence_violations(..., variable_form_mode=\"advisory\", descend_helpers=True)` unresolvable sites: edge_type 7 -> 1, evidence_type 12 -> 3, Symbol.kind 49 -> 11 (before -> after WI-nakur). What is left, by shape:\n\n1. Statement-level narrowing: yaml_ansible.py `evidence_type=key` under `if key in (...)` (filed separately as WI-janon-kifav-ritob-niduk-buduk-kapak-dunos-fudul: four unregistered values, one live-reproduced).\n2. Re-emission copies: yaml_ansible.py `edge_type=edge.edge_type` / `evidence_type=edge.evidence_type` (Jinja fan-out copies an edge the same analyzer made; the loop skips non-\"imports\" first). Acknowledged in test_depends_on_producer_sets._UNENUMERABLE_EDGE_TYPE_SITES.\n3. Collections of mutable collections: receiver_type_dispatch.py builds `index.setdefault(key, []).append((id, ev))` and reads `candidates[0]`; refused because the inner list can be filled through an alias the outer name's use-walk never sees.\n4. Cross-module producers: scip/edges.py emits `implements` for the rust_analyzer and scip_python analyzers, whose own modules only call scip_index_to_edges; the depends_on edge-type scan reads the analyzer's module only, so those two clause entries are hand-declared and unverified by the gate.\n5. Symbol.kind sites still unresolvable (11): swift.py x5 (`kind` param), clojure.py `kind`, graphql.py `op_type`, pony.py `type_kind`, rust_analyzer translate.py (Attribute), graphql_sdl.py (Attribute), cli.py (Call). Not examined individually.\n6. Also refused by design: public module-function parameters (callers may live in other modules), `self`/`cls` attributes, splats of non-tuple values, decorated functions other than lru_cache/cache.\n\nSeparately, a GOVERNANCE-FILE proposal (needs owner approval, .agent/** is governance): the fundamental-concept-audit playbook's Step 4.5 lists five producer-emit shapes and says to append a sixth with a file:line example. The sixth is \"value carried through data\" -- a loop over a list of tuples (scip/edges.py _RELATION_EDGE_TYPES), a helper's appended/returned tuples (linkers/lua_ffi.py _scan_lua_file_for_ffi_calls), a dict of tuples (linkers/napi.py export_map), a record-class field (dart.py _HeritageRef.edge_type). The L3 linter now traces it (value_flow), so the manual-grep instruction for shapes 3-5 is stale too."  # e5b2
    fields: {}  # e5b2
